sdata> -- Issue #70 / ADR-055: SAVE + implicit RUN association via the REPL path
sdata> -- specifically -- Ensure_Pending_Flushed's Run_Active_Program branch (a
sdata> -- pending LET queued in Active_Program_Vec) is a different code path from
sdata> -- the batch-style Step_Start flush repeat_save_implicit_run.cmd covers, but
sdata> -- both must consume the same Suppress_Next_Save_Flush flag so the
sdata> -- registered SAVE survives for SORT's own Execute_Commit_Step flush,
sdata> -- writing the sorted result (1,2,3,4), not the pre-sort table.
sdata> USE "tests/data/freq_select.csv"
Dataset opened: tests/data/freq_select.csv
sdata> LET Z = ID * -1
sdata> SAVE "tests/data/repl_implicit_run_save_out.csv"
sdata> SORT Z
RUN complete. 6 records and 4 variables processed.
SORT complete. 6 records and 4 variables processed.
Dataset saved: tests/data/repl_implicit_run_save_out.csv
sdata> NEW
sdata> USE "tests/data/repl_implicit_run_save_out.csv"
Dataset opened: tests/data/repl_implicit_run_save_out.csv
sdata> DISPLAY
REC# REGION$ PRODUCT$ ID Z 
1 West B 6.00000 -6.00000 
2 West B 5.00000 -5.00000 
3 West A 4.00000 -4.00000 
4 East B 3.00000 -3.00000 
5 East A 2.00000 -2.00000 
6 East A 1.00000 -1.00000 
sdata> QUIT
